Internal Identifier Compatibility Note

To preserve working installations, caches, artifacts, and Backlot project paths, StudioKat retains the following OpenMontage internal identifiers. These are implementation details, not user-facing brand:

- Directory name: `OpenMontage/` (repository root)
- Python configuration class: `OpenMontageConfig` (lib/config_model.py)
- Environment variables: `OPENMONTAGE_*` (cache dirs, feature flags, network allowances)
- Cache directory: `~/.openmontage/`
- Provider ID namespace: `provider="openmontage"` in tool registry entries
- Distribution package metadata (PyPI): may remain `openmontage` for install compatibility
- Checkpoint/artifact schemas: `schemas/**/*.json` reference `openmontage` in `$id` and examples

Changing these would break existing virtual environments, cached assets, rendered outputs, and Backlot board paths. They are intentionally left unchanged. User-facing surfaces (README, docs, CLI banners, UI titles, package description, agent guides) use the StudioKat brand.